  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'western-turquoise-squash-blossom-necklace-cowgirl-jewelry-southwestern-reproduct', '997536057', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/997536057/western-squash-blossom-turquoise?click_key=EuMhKOe2UTn7Xupp6hNYRoqS-xb4%3ALTe874f95b36565e1e2889a22f4afc11c951df3fa2&click_sum=ec197345&ls=a&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=turquoise+jewelry&ref=search_grid-970640-16-10&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&pro=1&cns=1&sts=1',
   'Western Turquoise Squash Blossom Necklace | Cowgirl Jewelry | Southwestern Reproduction', 'Make a statement with this bold Western turquoise squash blossom necklace, inspired by the iconic jewelry of the American Southwest. With its vibrant turquoise-colored stones, antiqued silver-tone finish and dramatic squash blossom silhouette, this piece has all the presence of classic Western jewelry without the collectible price tag. Style it with denim and boots for an effortless cowgirl look, layer it over a crisp white shirt, or wear it as the statement piece with a simple black dress. It''s substantial, eye-catching and made for anyone who loves jewelry with a strong Western personality. This is a Southwestern-style reproduction and is not Native American made. It is offered as a fashion jewelry alternative to traditional Native-made squash blossom necklaces. Perfect for: Western & cowgirl style • Rodeo wear • Country concerts • Ranch style • Southwestern outfits • Statement jewelry • Western gifts ***Please note that this blossom necklace is made of genuine turquoise magnesite stone with natural matrix so no two necklaces will look exactly the same.*** * Stones will vary in color and matrix. * Turquoise Magnesite Natural Stone (see below) * 28" necklace length with a 3" extension chain * 4" x 4" Naja * Navajo Style Pearls (pewter tone Pearls made of hard enamel) Please note: This is silver plate NOT STERLING SILVER What is Turquoise Magnesite Natural Stone and why do I use it… Magnesite is a beautiful gemstone that looks very similar to genuine Turquoise. When cut and polished into cabochons or beads it features a dark thread of veins or a web-like matrix across its surface, making it a beautiful gem to use as a substitute for real turquoise. Because this is a porous gem it can easily be dyed and polished to create bold and vibrant colors. It’s often dyed to a light blue color and because of its matrix it resembles turquoise so closely many people cannot tell the difference. Genuine turquoise has quadrupled in price in the last couple years and turquoise magne', 'statement-pieces',
